From 0bc6d301e751af82bc64bf828373245513e64654 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:36:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] player information: the decoder is said as graphics card or
 processor, with its interface

The overview page showed "hevc-vaapi (SW)" in the renders: the words came
from Kodi's own HW/SW variable, whose condition is
Player.Process(videohwdecoder) (CDataCacheCore::IsVideoHwDecoder(), set by
each codec: VAAPI and DRM PRIME say hardware, the software codec of ffmpeg
says not), and the sample data of the render lacked that value. The page was
not plain either: it gave the name of the codec object and not what is done.

The window system now publishes hades.video.decoding (hw or sw, from that
value) and hades.video.api (VAAPI, DRM PRIME, VDPAU or NVDEC, named from the
decoder name by DecoderApi(), tested), and the overview page says "Graphics
card (VAAPI)" or "Processor (software)" (strings 32817, 32818). The codec is
on its own row; the Video page keeps the technical name and Kodi's HW/SW.
